From: qualixxe <qualixxe@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: k9a-36-02-0a-mp-dsc: use the stock DSC slice geometry

The generated driver declares one 1080-wide slice at 10 bpp. The 10 bpp is
wrong: courbet's downstream panel dtsi
(dsi-panel-k9a-36-02-0a-mp-dsc-cmd.dtsi) and the dtbo dumped from the phone
both say

    qcom,mdss-dsc-slice-height = <12>;
    qcom,mdss-dsc-slice-width = <1080>;
    qcom,mdss-dsc-slice-per-pkt = <1>;
    qcom,mdss-dsc-bit-per-component = <10>;
    qcom,mdss-dsc-bit-per-pixel = <8>;

prepare() packs the PPS from this same struct, so at 10 bpp the panel decoder
is told a chunk size it was not initialised for. The panel's vendor DSC
register 0x91 is written with the stock payload by k9a_36_02_0a_mp_dsc_on()
and cannot be re-derived, so the PPS has to agree with it: 8 bpp.

The slice geometry stays one 1080-wide slice per line, matching
qcom,display-topology = <1 1 1> (one LM, one DSC, one INTF) in the stock dtbo.
dpu-dsc-single-slice.patch makes the DPU honour that instead of always
splitting the line over two DSC blocks.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-k9a-36-02-0a-mp-dsc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-k9a-36-02-0a-mp-dsc.c
@@ -339,17 +339,12 @@
 	ctx->dsc.dsc_version_major = 1;
 	ctx->dsc.dsc_version_minor = 1;
 
-	/* TODO: Pass slice_per_pkt = 1 */
+	/* Stock dtsi: one 1080-wide slice per line, 10 bpc, 8 bpp. */
 	ctx->dsc.slice_height = 12;
 	ctx->dsc.slice_width = 1080;
-	/*
-	 * TODO: hdisplay should be read from the selected mode once
-	 * it is passed back to drm_panel (in prepare?)
-	 */
-	WARN_ON(1080 % ctx->dsc.slice_width);
-	ctx->dsc.slice_count = 1080 / ctx->dsc.slice_width;
+	ctx->dsc.slice_count = 1;
 	ctx->dsc.bits_per_component = 10;
-	ctx->dsc.bits_per_pixel = 10 << 4; /* 4 fractional bits */
+	ctx->dsc.bits_per_pixel = 8 << 4; /* 4 fractional bits */
 	ctx->dsc.block_pred_enable = true;
 
 	ret = mipi_dsi_attach(dsi);
